From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 16:10:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] hw/display/edid: default the refresh rate to 60 Hz, not
 75

With no refresh rate from the display (D-Bus SetUIInfo carries none),
the generated EDID advertises its preferred mode at 75 Hz, so a guest
that takes the preferred mode runs at 75 Hz on a 60 Hz panel. A 4K
preferred mode at 75 Hz is also too fast for a detailed timing
descriptor, so it moves to a DisplayID block, which QEMU's own range
descriptor (<= 160 kHz) then excludes.

60 Hz matches the panels EVE's console drives. The real fix is for the
display to pass its refresh rate, which needs an addition to SetUIInfo.

Signed-off-by: Mikhail Malyshev <mike.malyshev@gmail.com>
---
 hw/display/edid-generate.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/display/edid-generate.c b/hw/display/edid-generate.c
index 2cb819675..dc8132efa 100644
--- a/hw/display/edid-generate.c
+++ b/hw/display/edid-generate.c
@@ -387,7 +387,7 @@ void qemu_edid_generate(uint8_t *edid, size_t size,
     uint8_t *dta = NULL;
     uint8_t *did = NULL;
     uint32_t width_mm, height_mm;
-    uint32_t refresh_rate = info->refresh_rate ? info->refresh_rate : 75000;
+    uint32_t refresh_rate = info->refresh_rate ? info->refresh_rate : 60000;
     uint32_t dpi = 100; /* if no width_mm/height_mm */
     uint32_t large_screen = 0;
 
